course: dictionary
lesson: 13301
title: Words with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show you which one the writer means. «The gravelly path crunched under our boots.» The path and the crunching are the clues. A path full of small stones makes that sound, so gravelly means covered with small stones here.
explain: The same word can describe a voice. «The old sailor spoke in a gravelly voice.» Sailor and voice are the clues. Here gravelly means low and rough, like stones rubbing together. Check it by putting your meaning into the sentence: does it still make sense?
explain: Gravel is a word you may know from parks and driveways. Gravelly soil has lots of small stones in it, so water drains through it fast. When a word has two meanings, ask which meaning the clues point to.
fact: Gravel means small stones.
fact: «Gravelly» means covered with or full of gravel.
fact: «Gravelly» can also describe a voice that is low and rough.
fact: A «gravelly voice» often belongs to an old sailor or a giant in stories.
fact: Gravelly soil drains water fast, so it does not stay wet for long.
exercise: «The gravelly path crunched under our feet.» What does gravelly mean here? | Smooth and wet like glass | Made of soft grass | *Covered with small stones | Very hot in the sun
exercise: «The old pirate had a gravelly voice that scared the children.» What does gravelly tell us about his voice? | High and squeaky | Loud and happy | Soft and sweet | *Low and rough
exercise: Gravelly soil lets rain drain away quickly. What is gravelly soil like? | Soft sand and moss | Thick, sticky mud | Covered in water | *Full of small stones
test: «She crunched across the gravelly yard.» What does gravelly mean? | Soft and wet with rain | *Covered with small stones | Painted bright green
test: «His gravelly voice made everyone look up.» What does gravelly describe? | A quick, light step | *A low, rough voice | A bowl of soup | A bright, shiny coat
exam: «The gravelly voice of the giant boomed across the valley.» What does gravelly mean here? | *Low and rough | Full of small stones | Shiny and new | Quick and light
